LC 454 — 4Sum II
Pattern:Hashing

Logic:

Store all possible sums of A + B.
Then check whether -(C + D) exists.

Algorithm:
Store A[i] + B[j] frequencies
For every C[i] + D[j]:
    check -(C[i] + D[j])
    add its frequency

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    int fourSumCount(vector<int>& A, vector<int>& B,
                     vector<int>& C, vector<int>& D) {
        unordered_map<int,int> mp;
        int ans = 0;

        for (int a : A)
            for (int b : B)
                mp[a + b]++;

        for (int c : C)
            for (int d : D)
                ans += mp[-(c + d)];

        return ans;
    }
};

EX:
A = [1,2]
B = [-2,-1]
C = [-1,2]
D = [0,2]

We need:

A + B + C + D = 0
Combination 1:
1 + (-2) + (-1) + 2
= 0 ✅
Combination 2:
2 + (-1) + (-1) + 0
= 0 ✅

Therefore:

2 valid combinations
        ↓
Answer = 2 ✅

Complexity:

Time: O(n²)
Space: O(n²)
